    "description": "On this full-day trip from London, you’ll get to explore the history of England’s landed gentry and recreate your favourite scenes from the hit TV series Downton Abbey. \r\n\r\nYou’ll get to travel to Oxfordshire to explore quintessential English villages such as Cogges, Bampton and Swinbrook. As you travel through the famous rolling limestone hills, your guide will provide entertaining stories and trivia about the TV series, pointing out familiar sights along the way. You’ll get to visit filming locations such as the church where Lady Mary and Matthew Crawley got married and the stone cottages and the fictional Grantham Arms too. \r\n\r\nIn the afternoon, you’ll have the chance to explore Blenheim Palace, one of the UK’s most magnificent aristocratic residences. As you wander around the lavish halls, your guide will share the history of Winston Churchill’s ancestral home.",
